  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe 3D Finish operation has no user-set toolpath direction. It cuts in a fixed direction that the user cannot change.\n\n## Expected\n\nAdd a direction angle setting to 3D Finish parallel. The user sets an angle (for example 90 degrees). The toolpath cuts parallel lines at that angle instead of only in the default direction.\n\n## Done means\n\n- 3D Finish parallel has a direction angle parameter in the operation panel.\n- The default angle is 0 degrees (unchanged behaviour).\n- On a flat-top model, the generated toolpath lines run at the set angle.\n- The pinning test covers angle 0 and angle 90.\n- No crash, no wrong output, no gouge for any valid angle.",
